WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.160
The layoffs continue, and&nbsp;
some are pretty… malicious.&nbsp;

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.760
Oracle is targeting workers with unvested stock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:12.480
CEOs are calling cut staff “low&nbsp;
performers” even when they aren’t.&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.640
Staff get layoff emails at 4am.
It’s all so weird.&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:22.160
And now, it seems to be backfiring.
In some cases, very drastically.&nbsp;

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.440
Doesn’t it feel like something’s&nbsp;
broken in corporate culture?&nbsp;

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:31.440
It feels like that unspoken contract, and&nbsp;
trust between staff and company, is breaking.&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:41.920
This is what happens when your&nbsp;
employees start to hate you.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.000
We’re in a strange time right now.&nbsp;

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.360
All these layoffs aren’t because companies&nbsp;
are struggling, it’s actually the opposite.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:53.920
“While AI leaders insist that their&nbsp;
tools will empower and augment workers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.800
instead of displacing them, several&nbsp;
companies, especially those in tech,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.480
have initiated mass layoffs and are&nbsp;
prioritizing spending on AI above workers.”&nbsp;

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:10.000
These companies are making more profit than ever,&nbsp;
and this stage of layoffs is about companies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:17.440
“consolidating” or focusing on “efficiency”.
And as we’ll see, that’s not entirely true…

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:23.120
Cloudflare generated $639.8 million in&nbsp;
just the first three months of 2026,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:28.560
a 34% increase from the previous year.
Two months later, on May 7, Cloudflare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.400
laid off 1,000 employees to rely&nbsp;
more on AI. About 20% of the company.&nbsp;

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.680
Some who were fired weren’t even given a reason.&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.040
IBM's CEO Krishna promised more grad&nbsp;
hiring, then laid off thousands days later.&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.560
Several CEOs have even attended graduation&nbsp;
ceremonies to give speeches promoting AI,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.040
including current and former Google&nbsp;
CEOs Sundar Pichai and Eric Schmidt.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.480
And there’s more,
Pinterest announced cutting 15%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:11.360
of staff to invest in AI, out of 4,700 employees.
Atlassian laid off 1,600 people, called it an "AI&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:17.040
investment," and its stock rose about 2%.
Intel’s also restructuring and eliminating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.920
more than 25,000 positions, about&nbsp;
1/5 of their entire headcount.&nbsp;

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.480
But one of the strangest is Meta.
First, theirs was amongst the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:33.120
biggest layoffs. 8,000 in May 2026.
This was also, out of nowhere. Employees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.400
woke up to termination emails sent at 4am.
‘Yesterday I was training up my new pod&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:43.760
engineer, glad I managed to squeeze&nbsp;
in everything. Today. I'm laid off,’&nbsp;

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:48.000
And to make matters worse,&nbsp;
leaked audio reveals more.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.680
Not great.
More than 1,000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.440
employees signed an internal petition demanding&nbsp;
the company stop using that data for AI training.&nbsp;

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:38.000
But, things are a bit more nuanced.
Regarding those layoffs, Meta is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.280
offering pretty generous severance packages and&nbsp;
healthcare support, better than most tech layoffs.&nbsp;

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:48.640
They’ve also reassigned more than 7,000 workers to&nbsp;
new teams centred around artificial intelligence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:53.040
instead of cutting them.
But some of these get much worse.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.360
Before we get to that, I’d like to talk&nbsp;
to you about today’s sponsor ZocDoc.&nbsp;

